---
# The bounds (one queued message, one failure row, one chip) end every
# behaviour in a quiet composer: that is rest, not a deadlock.
deadlock_detection: false
---

# The web composer as the person sees it (web/src/app.tsx Thread: the
# draft, send/enqueue/deliver, attach/take/expand, the failure rows and
# the queue, the key hints; mention.tsx Mentions and triggerAt;
# skills.tsx SkillPicker; select.tsx Select for the model and effort
# pickers in the composer toolbar).
#
# Two sessions. A is the one this flow drives: its turns run, fail,
# queue and get archived. B is a quiet idle session that is here to show
# the draft is per session (localStorage bough:draft:<id>): the person
# only types in it, clears it and switches back.
#
# Fields (all on the Composer role; see go/tests/model/README.md):
#   session   the thread on screen (#/s/<id>): a | b
#   status    A's row status: idle | running | archived (B stays idle)
#   pending   A has a sent, unlanded prompt: the optimistic row and the
#             "Sending" status from deliver()
#   queued    A's queued messages (sessionStorage), 0..1
#   failed    A has a "Not sent" row with Retry, Edit and Discard
#   draft_a   A's draft: "" | typed | multi (a Shift+Enter newline) |
#             pasted (a "[Pasted text #1 +N lines]" or uploaded
#             "[Image #1]" tag) | uploading ("Attaching image…") |
#             lost (a tag whose file never arrived: "not attached")
#   draft_b   B's draft: "" | typed
#   popover   the one open popover: none | slash (the / picker at the
#             caret) | mention (the @ picker) | skills (the Skills
#             button's dialog) | model | effort (the toolbar Selects)
#   listing   what the open popover shows: loading | list | error.
#             A caret picker or Skills: "Couldn't load … Retry". A
#             Select: a pick the server refused, said in the Select,
#             which stays open.
#   focus     composer | popover (the Skills filter, a Select) |
#             elsewhere (a toolbar button, the page)
#   placeholder_sent
#             the last message sent, steered or queued carried a tag
#             whose file never arrived, as its literal "[Image #1]"
#
# Derived in view(), read straight off the page:
#   shown         the draft in the textarea (a's or b's)
#   composer_on   the textarea is enabled (A archived: "Read-only")
#   send_label    Send | Steer, the primary button's name
#   send_enabled  the primary button is enabled
#   queue_shown   the Queue button is there
#   stop_shown    the Stop button is there (A's turn is live)
#   edit_enabled  the failure row's Edit button is enabled
#   status_word   the composer foot's word, by phase: "" | sending
#                 ("Sending", then "Waiting" once taken) | running
#                 ("Waiting" until output, then "Working")
#   hint          the key hints: send | live | steer, or hidden while a
#                 caret picker owns the keys
#
# Where this departs from the code, and why:
# - Steering and the queue's order are steer_queue.fizz; the stop
#   handshake is stop_interrupt.fizz; the catalogue load behind the
#   model picker is model_effort_controls.fizz. Here a steer is the
#   draft clearing while the turn runs, and Stop ends the turn and may
#   put its prompt back.
# - One extra at a time: a popover, a chip, a multi-line draft, a
#   failure row, a queued message, an archive or a visit to B each
#   start only from a calm composer (A on screen, a plain draft, none of
#   the others), and cross the core (A's status, a send in flight) only
#   where that changes the screen: a caret picker while running (Esc
#   shuts it, not the turn), a chip while running (Queue waits for the
#   upload), the Skills and model pickers while archived. Crossing
#   everything made 3845 paths, one browser test each.
# - A click away from a popover is Escape here: it shuts the same way.
# - The picker's 200 ms "slow" (a fast load shows nothing) is not a
#   state: loading is the panel blank or saying "Loading…".
# - An upload never spans a switch (Switch waits for it): the Thread
#   that started it is unmounted and nothing on screen shows it.
# - The viewport is wide: on a phone the pickers move under Settings.
# - Enqueue refuses a draft whose tag lost its file, as send() does.
#   The code's enqueue() does not check that today and queues the
#   literal "[Image #1]": this spec says what the page must do.

role Composer:
    action Init:
        self.session = "a"
        self.status = "idle"
        self.pending = False
        self.queued = 0
        self.failed = False
        self.draft_a = ""
        self.draft_b = ""
        self.popover = "none"
        self.listing = "list"
        self.focus = "composer"
        self.placeholder_sent = False
        self.view()

    # What the page renders from the fields above. atomic: a plain func
    # is a yield point, and the assertions would see new fields beside
    # the old view.
    atomic func view():
        on_a = self.session == "a"
        running = on_a and self.status == "running"
        self.shown = self.draft_a if on_a else self.draft_b
        self.composer_on = not (on_a and self.status == "archived")
        self.send_label = "Steer" if running else "Send"
        blank = self.shown == ""
        self.send_enabled = self.composer_on and not blank and self.shown != "uploading"
        self.queue_shown = running and not blank
        self.stop_shown = running or (on_a and self.pending)
        # The failure row's Edit: disabled while a draft is there.
        self.edit_enabled = on_a and self.failed and blank
        if running:
            self.status_word = "running"
        elif self.stop_shown:
            self.status_word = "sending"
        else:
            self.status_word = ""
        if self.popover == "slash" or self.popover == "mention":
            self.hint = "hidden"
        elif running:
            self.hint = "steer"
        elif self.stop_shown:
            self.hint = "live"
        else:
            self.hint = "send"

    atomic func set_draft(d):
        if self.session == "a":
            self.draft_a = d
        else:
            self.draft_b = d

    atomic func live():
        return self.session == "a" and (self.status == "running" or self.pending)

    # Nothing extra on screen: A open, no popover, no chip, no failure
    # row, no queued message. See "One extra at a time" above.
    atomic func calm():
        return (self.session == "a" and self.popover == "none" and not self.failed
                and self.queued == 0 and self.draft_a in ["", "typed"])

    # A toolbar popover opens over an empty draft with no turn live: its
    # crossing with a running turn or a draft shows nothing new.
    atomic func toolbar_ok():
        return self.status != "running" and not self.pending and self.draft_a == ""

    # ---- typing ----

    # A word at the caret. A space ends any / or @ token, so an open
    # caret picker shuts.
    atomic action Type:
        require self.composer_on and self.focus == "composer"
        require (self.shown == "" and self.popover == "none") or self.popover in ["slash", "mention"]
        if self.shown == "":
            self.set_draft("typed")
        self.popover = "none"
        self.listing = "list"
        self.view()

    # Shift+Enter: a newline in the draft. (With a caret picker open it
    # is a newline too, and shuts the picker as Type does.) A multi-line
    # draft is a leaf here: it is sent or cleared, and nothing else opens
    # over it.
    atomic action Newline:
        c = self.calm()
        require c and self.composer_on and self.focus == "composer"
        require self.draft_a == "typed" and self.status == "idle" and not self.pending
        self.draft_a = "multi"
        self.view()

    # "/" or "@" starting a word opens the caret picker over it. The
    # sigil is text: the draft is no longer blank.
    atomic action TypeTrigger:
        c = self.calm()
        require c and not self.pending and self.composer_on and self.focus == "composer"
        kind = oneof ["slash", "mention"]
        self.draft_a = "typed"
        self.popover = kind
        self.listing = "loading"
        self.view()

    # ---- a popover's list ----

    atomic fair<strong> action ListLoads:
        require self.popover in ["slash", "mention", "skills"] and self.listing == "loading"
        self.listing = "list"

    atomic action ListFails:
        require self.popover in ["slash", "mention", "skills"] and self.listing == "loading"
        self.listing = "error"

    # "Couldn't load … Retry". The caret picker's Retry keeps the
    # composer focused (its mousedown is prevented).
    atomic action RetryList:
        require self.popover in ["slash", "mention", "skills"] and self.listing == "error"
        self.listing = "loading"

    # Enter/Tab or a click on a row. A caret pick replaces the token; a
    # Skills pick writes "/name " at the lead. Both hand the keys back to
    # the composer. On an archived session a Skills pick still writes the
    # draft, but the disabled textarea cannot take focus.
    atomic action PickItem:
        require self.popover in ["slash", "mention", "skills"] and self.listing == "list"
        self.draft_a = "typed"
        self.popover = "none"
        self.focus = "composer" if self.composer_on else "elsewhere"
        self.view()

    # Escape in a popover closes that popover only: never the turn, never
    # the thread. A caret picker leaves focus in the composer; the Skills
    # dialog and a Select give it back to their button.
    atomic action Escape:
        require self.popover != "none"
        self.focus = "composer" if self.popover in ["slash", "mention"] else "elsewhere"
        self.popover = "none"
        self.listing = "list"
        self.view()

    # ---- the toolbar ----

    # The Skills button: opening moves focus into its filter, a second
    # click closes it onto the button. It is offered on an archived
    # session too (see the notes on this flow's report).
    atomic action ClickSkills:
        if self.popover == "skills":
            self.popover = "none"
            self.listing = "list"
            self.focus = "elsewhere"
        else:
            c = self.calm()
            t = self.toolbar_ok()
            require c and t
            self.popover = "skills"
            self.listing = "loading"
            self.focus = "popover"
        self.view()

    # The model or effort Select: a click opens it with focus inside, a
    # second closes it onto its button.
    atomic action ClickSetting:
        which = oneof ["model", "effort"]
        if self.popover == which:
            self.popover = "none"
            self.focus = "elsewhere"
        else:
            c = self.calm()
            t = self.toolbar_ok()
            require c and t
            self.popover = which
            self.focus = "popover"
        self.listing = "list"
        self.view()

    # A pick the server takes closes the Select onto its button. On an
    # archived session the server refuses it (409) and the Select stays
    # open saying so.
    atomic action PickSetting:
        require self.popover in ["model", "effort"] and self.listing == "list"
        if self.status == "archived":
            self.listing = "error"
        else:
            self.popover = "none"
            self.focus = "elsewhere"

    # ---- focus ----

    # Alt+I, the skip link, or a click in the textarea, with no popover
    # open (a click there shuts one as Escape does).
    atomic action FocusComposer:
        require self.composer_on and self.focus != "composer" and self.popover == "none"
        self.focus = "composer"
        self.view()

    # ---- attachments ----

    # A long paste becomes "[Pasted text #1 +N lines]" at once; an image
    # becomes "[Image #1]" and uploads. A paste never opens a picker over
    # text nobody typed.
    atomic action Paste:
        c = self.calm()
        require c and not self.pending and self.composer_on and self.focus == "composer"
        kind = oneof ["pasted", "uploading"]
        self.draft_a = kind
        self.view()

    atomic fair<strong> action UploadDone:
        require self.draft_a == "uploading"
        self.draft_a = "pasted"
        self.view()

    atomic action UploadFails:
        require self.draft_a == "uploading"
        self.draft_a = "lost"
        self.view()

    # Select all and delete (a tag deleted on its own drops its
    # attachment the same way).
    atomic action ClearDraft:
        require self.composer_on and self.focus == "composer" and self.popover == "none"
        require self.shown not in ["", "uploading"]
        self.set_draft("")
        self.view()

    # ---- sending ----

    # Enter in the composer (a caret picker owns Enter, even empty or
    # loading, so none is open) or a click on Send / Steer. While A is
    # live it steers; otherwise it sends and the
    # optimistic row says "Sending". A tag whose file is gone is never
    # sent as its placeholder: the draft stays and the page names it.
    atomic action Send:
        require self.session == "a" and self.send_enabled and self.popover == "none"
        if self.draft_a != "lost":
            self.placeholder_sent = self.draft_a == "lost"
            live = self.live()
            if not live:
                self.pending = True
            self.draft_a = ""
            self.view()

    # Cmd/Ctrl+Enter or the Queue button while A runs: the message waits
    # for the turn to end. Refused like Send for a tag that lost its file.
    atomic action Enqueue:
        require self.session == "a" and self.queue_shown and self.draft_a != "uploading"
        require self.popover == "none" and self.queued == 0 and not self.failed
        if self.draft_a != "lost":
            self.placeholder_sent = self.draft_a == "lost"
            self.queued = 1
            self.draft_a = ""
            self.view()

    # The flush effect hands the queue's head to deliver() once A is idle
    # with nothing unlanded. It runs in A's mounted Thread only.
    atomic fair<strong> action Flush:
        require self.session == "a" and self.status == "idle"
        require not self.pending and self.queued > 0
        self.queued = 0
        self.pending = True
        self.view()

    # ---- the server ----

    # The prompt is recorded and its turn starts.
    atomic fair<strong> action Land:
        require self.pending
        self.pending = False
        self.status = "running"
        self.view()

    # POST /send answered with an error: the optimistic row goes and a
    # "Not sent" row keeps the message with its cause.
    atomic action SendFails:
        c = self.calm()
        require self.pending and c
        self.pending = False
        self.failed = True
        self.view()

    atomic fair<strong> action Finish:
        require self.status == "running"
        self.status = "idle"
        self.view()

    # Esc in the composer with no popover open, or the Stop button. A
    # turn stopped before any reply puts its prompt back in an empty
    # draft.
    atomic action Stop:
        require self.session == "a" and self.status == "running"
        require self.popover == "none"
        self.status = "idle"
        if self.draft_a == "":
            restored = oneof ["", "typed"]
            self.draft_a = restored
        self.view()

    # ---- the failure row ----

    # Retry resends the same request (a steer if A is live meanwhile).
    # Archived, the server refuses it and the row stays.
    atomic action Retry:
        require self.session == "a" and self.failed and self.status != "archived"
        self.failed = False
        live = self.live()
        if not live:
            self.pending = True
        self.view()

    # Edit puts the message back, only into an empty draft (the button
    # is disabled otherwise): two prompts are never glued together.
    atomic action EditFailed:
        require self.edit_enabled
        self.failed = False
        self.draft_a = "typed"
        self.focus = "composer"
        self.view()

    atomic action Discard:
        require self.session == "a" and self.failed
        self.failed = False
        self.view()

    # ---- archive and switching ----

    # Archived from the header's settings or another client, from a calm
    # composer. The textarea is disabled and focus falls out of it; the
    # draft is kept.
    atomic action Archive:
        c = self.calm()
        require c and self.status == "idle" and not self.pending
        self.status = "archived"
        self.focus = "elsewhere"
        self.view()

    # The Unarchive button on the composer's note, or another client.
    atomic action Unarchive:
        require self.status == "archived" and self.popover == "none"
        self.status = "idle"
        self.view()

    # A click on the other session's row. Each draft stays with its own
    # session; every popover belongs to the thread left behind.
    atomic action Switch:
        c = self.calm()
        require self.session == "b" or (c and self.status == "idle" and not self.pending)
        self.session = "b" if self.session == "a" else "a"
        self.popover = "none"
        self.listing = "list"
        self.focus = "elsewhere"
        self.view()

action Init:
    composer = Composer()

# ---- what is always true on screen ----

# The textarea shows the open session's own draft, never the other's.
always assertion DraftIsTheSessions:
    c = composer
    return c.shown == (c.draft_a if c.session == "a" else c.draft_b)

# Exactly one owner of the keys: a toolbar popover holds focus, a caret
# picker leaves it in the composer, and nothing else holds a popover's.
always assertion FocusFollowsPopover:
    p = composer.popover
    if p in ["skills", "model", "effort"]:
        return composer.focus == "popover"
    if p in ["slash", "mention"]:
        return composer.focus == "composer"
    return composer.focus != "popover"

# A read-only composer is never focused and never has a caret picker.
always assertion ArchivedIsReadOnly:
    if composer.composer_on:
        return True
    return composer.focus != "composer" and composer.popover not in ["slash", "mention"]

# No send control is enabled that would fail: Send needs a draft, a
# live composer and no upload in flight; Queue shows only while A runs.
always assertion NoControlThatWouldFail:
    c = composer
    if c.send_enabled and (c.shown in ["", "uploading"] or not c.composer_on):
        return False
    if c.queue_shown and not (c.session == "a" and c.status == "running" and c.shown != ""):
        return False
    return True

# A live turn always says so, picker open or not; a quiet one does not.
always assertion LiveTurnHasStatus:
    c = composer
    if c.session == "a" and (c.status == "running" or c.pending):
        return c.status_word != "" and c.stop_shown
    return c.status_word == "" and not c.stop_shown

# The primary button says Steer exactly while A's turn runs.
always assertion SteerWhileRunning:
    running = composer.session == "a" and composer.status == "running"
    return (composer.send_label == "Steer") == running

# The key hints step aside only for a caret picker.
always assertion HintsHiddenOnlyForPicker:
    return (composer.hint == "hidden") == (composer.popover in ["slash", "mention"])

# A tag whose file never arrived is never sent, steered or queued as its
# placeholder text.
always assertion NoPlaceholderSent:
    return not composer.placeholder_sent

# Leaving a session and coming back keeps each draft as it was.
transition assertion DraftsSurviveSwitch(before, after):
    b = before.composer
    a = after.composer
    if a.session != b.session:
        return a.draft_a == b.draft_a and a.draft_b == b.draft_b
    return True

# Edit on a failure row is offered only over an empty draft: a message
# put back never lands on (or replaces) one already being written.
always assertion EditOnlyOverEmpty:
    return not composer.edit_enabled or (composer.failed and composer.shown == "")

# ---- what always ends ----

# "Sending" does not hang: the prompt lands or its failure row shows.
always eventually assertion SendingResolves:
    return not composer.pending

# A popover's list does not stay loading (it may fail; Retry is yours).
always eventually assertion ListSettles:
    return composer.listing != "loading"

# The queue drains once A's turn ends while A is on screen.
always eventually assertion QueueDrains:
    return composer.queued == 0 or composer.status != "idle" or composer.session != "a"
